Implement run(api). api.inspect('state') returns detached current state, costing one unit. api.apply(operation) atomically executes a documented operation and returns updated state. A failed precondition or safety invariant invalidates the case, even if caught. Do not access API internals. Different valid complete plans are accepted.

Validate and health-check a replacement release. Preserve sticky sessions on successful cutover and retire the old instance. If unhealthy, discard the replacement and retain old service. Resume any paused batch workers on both paths.

Operations (all requires predicates must hold):
- verify_artifact: requires {}; effects {"signed": true}; cost 1.
- pause_batch_workers: requires {"capacity": false, "workers_paused": false}; effects {"capacity": true, "workers_paused": true}; cost 2.
- allocate_green: requires {"capacity": true, "signed": true}; effects {"green": true}; cost 1.
- warm_green: requires {"green": true}; effects {"warm": true}; cost 1.
- probe_health: requires {"warm": true}; effects {"probed": true}; cost 1.
- drain_sticky_sessions: requires {"probed": true, "blue": true}; effects {"drained": true}; cost 1.
- switch_traffic: requires {"probed": true, "healthy": true}; effects {"new_traffic": true}; cost 1.
- retire_blue: requires {"new_traffic": true}; effects {"blue": false}; cost 1.
- resume_workers_after_release: requires {"blue": false}; effects {"workers_paused": false}; cost 1.
- discard_green: requires {"probed": true, "healthy": false, "new_traffic": false}; effects {"green": false, "warm": false}; cost 1.
- resume_workers_after_abort: requires {"green": false, "blue": true}; effects {"workers_paused": false}; cost 1.
- record_release_audit: requires {"probed": true, "workers_paused": false, "new_traffic": true, "blue": false, "green": true, "audited": false}; effects {"audited": true}; cost 1.

Safety invariants:
[
  {
    "name": "session_continuity",
    "when": {
      "new_traffic": true,
      "sticky_sessions": true
    },
    "requires": {
